1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,756
Agents are buying from your store.

2
00:00:03,806 --> 00:00:07,469
When one goes wrong, who's at fault?

3
00:00:07,519 --> 00:00:13,656
Undo answers that, and settles it through PayPal in minutes.

4
00:00:13,706 --> 00:00:16,234
My agent shops for a tee.

5
00:00:16,284 --> 00:00:19,844
I approve the exact item on PayPal,

6
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:26,650
and Undo hashes what I approved into the PayPal order's custom ID.

7
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,188
A navy tee shows up.

8
00:00:29,238 --> 00:00:31,514
The agent opens a claim,

9
00:00:31,564 --> 00:00:36,069
and Undo asks for a photo with a one-time code.

10
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:41,109
The vision model reads the color, size tag and code.

11
00:00:41,159 --> 00:00:45,857
A deterministic fault engine compares it with the

12
00:00:45,907 --> 00:00:49,637
PayPal order: the merchant is at fault.

13
00:00:49,687 --> 00:00:52,932
The store's rules make the offers.

14
00:00:52,982 --> 00:00:58,650
The agent picks the keep-it refund, and PayPal confirms it.

15
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:01,546
Now a delegated purchase.

16
00:01:01,596 --> 00:01:06,047
The person approved a spending limit for a size M

17
00:01:06,097 --> 00:01:10,271
tee; the agent chose later and bought a large.

18
00:01:10,321 --> 00:01:14,588
Nobody approved that, so the agent is at fault,

19
00:01:14,638 --> 00:01:20,650
and the agent platform pays the buyer back through PayPal Payouts.

20
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,115
"My agent bought this without asking me."

21
00:01:25,165 --> 00:01:29,829
But the person approved this exact cart on PayPal,

22
00:01:29,879 --> 00:01:34,637
the hash still matches, and the right item arrived.

23
00:01:34,687 --> 00:01:39,822
Denied, with reasons, and a link to escalate to PayPal,

24
00:01:39,872 --> 00:01:42,650
which stays the final arbiter.

25
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:46,666
A hundred-and-twenty-dollar jacket.

26
00:01:46,716 --> 00:01:52,130
The merchant asks the AI assistant to refund it in full.

27
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,960
The assistant can only draft.

28
00:01:55,010 --> 00:01:59,449
The policy evaluator blocks the draft: keep-it

29
00:01:59,499 --> 00:02:03,060
refunds are capped at thirty percent.

30
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:10,086
The thirty-six dollar refund the rules allow goes to the approval queue,

31
00:02:10,136 --> 00:02:12,038
and one tap pays it.

32
00:02:12,088 --> 00:02:15,161
No AI ever touches a money tool,

33
00:02:15,211 --> 00:02:19,650
and every step is on a hash-chained audit log.

34
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:24,869
If the buyer goes to PayPal anyway, Undo answers there.

35
00:02:24,919 --> 00:02:28,480
Here the store was at fault, so it accepts,

36
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:30,748
and PayPal closes the case.

37
00:02:30,798 --> 00:02:36,039
Thirteen scenarios, measured in the sandbox: every fault right,

38
00:02:36,089 --> 00:02:39,650
every remedy right, zero policy violations.
